---
title: "HCML Monitoring Portal: the life of one cached answer"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    %% core/cache.ts. A key is Missing, Fresh, in its stale window, or Expired.
    %% The stale window and the old copy after a failure are asked for by the caller, not always on.

    [*] --> Missing
    Missing --> Fresh: first call fetches, and callers that arrive meanwhile share that one fetch
    Fresh --> StaleWindow: lifetime passed, and a stale window was asked for
    Fresh --> Expired: lifetime passed, no stale window
    StaleWindow --> Fresh: the one background refresh succeeds
    StaleWindow --> StaleWindow: a failed refresh is tried again a minute later
    StaleWindow --> Expired: the window passes
    Expired --> Fresh: a fetch in the foreground succeeds
    Expired --> OldCopy: the fetch fails and the caller asked for an old copy
    OldCopy --> OldCopy: for a minute, calls get the old copy again without a fetch
    OldCopy --> Expired: after that minute the next call tries again
    Fresh --> Missing: invalidate drops it, or it is evicted as least recently used

    note right of Fresh
        Answered at once while its age is under the lifetime.
    end note
    note right of StaleWindow
        Answered at once with the old copy, with a header that says a refresh is running.
    end note
    note right of OldCopy
        Answered with the last copy, with a header that says it is old and how old.
    end note
